A||N||4||Elenor84||Where does the engine tach wire go?(4cyl)||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||12-11-2001||02:29 AM||||Hey guys...just alittle wile ago I had my car in the shop to get my coil and everything rewired(accel),but they could not find were to put this one wire.  So I got in and started her up and the tach didn't work.  So I suspect that the mistery wire is the tach wire.  Now does anyone know were I'm supposed to splice it into?  Thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||johnt671||12-11-2001||08:22 AM||||Look at the coil.  The wire plugged to the coil on the lower left terminal if I remember right.  You may see where the wire was cut.  I'd go and check mine but I replaced the coil with an MSD.<p>[This message has been edited by johnt671 (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||12-11-2001||02:26 PM||||I also installed an aftermarket coil...accel...so that changes everything doesen't it?||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnt671||12-11-2001||02:48 PM||||I went with an MSD GM blaster coil and before I installed the 6A system the tach plug was the same as stock, the lower left plug as you look at the the coil in the stock location.  Don't know if Accel makes one like that.  If its a different style it may have a marked terminal for the tach.  If not the feed for the tach should go to a + (positive) terminal on the coil.<p>[This message has been edited by johnt671 (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Elenor84||12-11-2001||07:36 PM||||Thats all?  Just put it to the positive on my coil?  Sweet.  Thx Guys!  I'll give that a try tonight!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
